    "Printed: 4'-0\" (PT 4'-1 1/2\") top = 1'-8 3/4\" + web + 1'-8 3/4\"; 3\" tip thickness; 1 3/4\" underside taper from tip to web face; r = 10\" web fillets; r = 2 1/2\" (typ) at the flange-tip and bottom-flange-edge corners; 6 1/8\" bottom edge; 6 3/8\" bottom taper rising to the web face over 1'-7 1/4\"; 3'-9\" (PT 3'-10 1/2\") bottom; 3/4\" soffit chamfer.",
    "Every radius is implemented as the unique tangent arc between the two straight lines it joins (16 segments). The top outer flange corners are drawn square.",
    "Printed area is ~2.2 in^2 below the otherwise uniform +39 in^2 (pretensioned) / +48 in^2 (PT) per-6-in increment of the neighbouring rows, and I is ~0.1% above the computed value while the neighbouring rows are ~0.2% below; the odd 6'-6\"/7'-6\"/8'-6\"/9'-6\" rows appear to come from a slightly different calculation. Pinned individually."
   ],
